# Top-level RUNTIME deps for services/ai-backend. Regenerate the lock:
#   cd services/ai-backend && .venv/bin/pip-compile --generate-hashes --resolver=backtracking requirements.in -o requirements.txt
#
# Only DECLARED dependencies belong here. `requirements.txt` is generated from
# this file and carries the full transitive closure with hashes, installed with
# `--require-hashes` — the same gate services/backend and services/backend-facade
# already have. It exists because the hand-maintained flat pin list it replaced
# could not see what it did not list: `mcp==1.29.0` silently pulled jsonschema,
# httpx-sse, referencing, rpds-py and jsonschema-specifications, none of which
# were pinned, so `pip-audit` and the published SBOM never saw them either.
#
# Test tooling lives in `requirements-dev.in`. Keep it that way: `pip-audit` and
# the CycloneDX SBOM step in `.github/workflows/ci-ai-backend.yml` read
# `requirements.txt` ALONE so they describe only what actually ships.
#
# Keep the pins here in sync with `pyproject.toml`'s `[project] dependencies` —
# that metadata is what `pip install ./services/ai-backend` resolves, and a
# version that disagrees with the lock is a divergence nobody sees until deploy.

